==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|zakah}}, {{l|en|zakaah}}, {{l|en|zakāh}}, {{l|en|zikat}}/[[Zikat]], {{l|en|Zikât}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fa|زکات|tr=zakât}}, from {{derived|en|ar|زَكَاة}}, from earlier Arabic {{m|ar|زَكَوٰة|tr=zakāh}}. {{root|en|ar|ز ك و}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɒt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|Islam}} [[almsgiving|Almsgiving]], one of the [[five pillars]] of [[Islam]].
#* '''1958-1994''', {{w|Hamilton Gibb}} & CF Beckingham, in ''The Travels of Ibn Battutah'', Folio Society 2012, p. 27:
#*: Amongst these stations is the well-known place called Qatya, where '''''zakat''''' is collected from the merchants, their goods are examined and their baggage most rigorously searched.

